@package Network
The `Runtime` package provides the coroutine scheduling and asynchronous
operation primitives used to execute and coordinate Mint coroutines.

A {Runtime.Scheduler} manages the execution of spawned coroutines. Coroutines can
suspend their execution by providing an {Runtime.Operation} and are resumed when
the operation completes. Operations provide the mechanism for representing
work that may complete asynchronously.

Spawning a coroutine returns a {Runtime.Promise} that can be used to observe its
completion and retrieve its result. Promises allow the caller to coordinate
with spawned coroutines without directly managing their execution.

The package provides the following core abstractions:
* {Runtime.Scheduler} manages coroutine scheduling and execution.
* {Runtime.Operation} represents an asynchronous operation that a coroutine can suspend on.
* {Runtime.Promise} represents the eventual completion and result of a spawned coroutine.

Together, these abstractions provide the foundation for asynchronous and
concurrent programming with Mint coroutines.

```mn
let scheduler = Runtime.Scheduler()

let promise = scheduler.spawn(def [...]() {
    return await scheduler.suspend(MyOperation())
})

scheduler.run()

let result = promise.get()
```
